      "rationality_summary": "Get on: `( ((status = get_command((& command) , (& prio) , (& ratio))) + 0) )`. Operator `u-ORAN` in function `dispatch`. Semantic hypothesis: a constant rewrite may leave behaviour unchanged for the value domains this harness exercises, or the constant may be dominated by later logic. Build-view fragment (truncated): 'void dispatch(void)\\n{\\n int command, prio, status;\\n float ratio;\\n struct process *process;\\n while @\\n((status = get_command(&command, &prio, &ratio)) > 0)@\\n {\\n  schedule(command, prio, ratio);\\n }\\n if (status < 0)\\n  exit_here(status);\\n exit_here(0);\\n}'. After 5 mutation-directed probes that varied inputs around literals/boundaries from Get on: while keeping oracle = original runner (CUNIT_CAPTURE), the mutant remained Alive. Residual doubt: multi-function scenarios or encodings outside this CSV schema might still distinguish the mutant; treating as possible equivalent for this operator-adequate suite under the current interface.",
